N2  - Summary Earth observation (EO) views and collects information about the Earth and objects on it from space. EO can be performed passively with the Sun as the light source and actively using radars. In optical EO, sunlight reflected from the targets contains rich information over different wavelengths in the visible and infrared spectrum. Such information can be extracted by sensors with multiple wavelength capabilities and analyzed. Synthetic aperture radars on satellites use microwave pulses to interrogate target areas, collect and analyze the returned signals. Entrepreneurs are offering commercial applications to service different sectors.
